    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="0727" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2653: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-08T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 8,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 8—10:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>35. Referring to the Legation’s telegram of January 19, 8 p.m.<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d615-f1"/> Four Ministers offered 5,000,000 pound sterling loan on
                    three conditions specified. Chinese Government has replied accepting conditions
                    and asking immediate advance of 7,000,000 dollars pending completion of
                    negotiations for large loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d615-f1" n="83" xml:id="d615-f1-content">
                <p>Probably refers to Legation’s undated telegram, <ref target="#pg621">p.
                    621</ref>.</p>
            </note>
